            <div xml:id="d876">

                <pb facs="0825" n="817" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg817"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/2295a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassodar in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-09-26T18:00:00-04:00">September 26, 1940—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>366. Unless you perceive objection, please seek an interview with the Minister
                    for Foreign Affairs at the earliest practicable moment and say that this
                    Government has received information to the effect that certain Japanese military
                    elements at Shanghai propose that Japanese armed forces forcibly occupy the
                    French Concession there within the immediate future. Say that the Government of
                    the United States views this report with serious concern both because of our
                    general interest in the maintenance of the <hi rendition="#italic">status
                        quo</hi> except as changes may be and are brought about through orderly
                    processes with due consideration for the rights and legitimate interests of all
                    concerned, <pb facs="0826" n="818" xml:id="pg818"/> and because of the residence
                    in the French Concession of a considerable part of the American community at
                    Shanghai. Express hope that there is no foundation in fact for the report in
                    question and request information in regard thereto.</p>
                <p>Please repeat to Shanghai for repetition by Shanghai to Chungking and
                    Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
